WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.759 --> 00:00:19.980
December 2016 Italy's populist
opposition is shaking up the

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.910
establishment

00:00:36.579 --> 00:00:41.370
They're days away from a referendum that

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:46.140
could spell the end for the Italian
government and make it the latest domino

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:52.309
in the toppling international order
Around the world populist leaders are

00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:56.930
connecting with voters fed up with
politics as usual and exploiting anger

00:00:56.930 --> 00:01:01.370
at an establishment out of touch with
ordinary people but giving voice to

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:06.020
people's frustrations is one thing
offering them real answers is quite

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.380
another

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:29.490
Jeff Segal grew up in New York but moved
to Italy 40 years ago

00:01:38.159 --> 00:01:44.219
He's trying to drum up support ahead of the referendum

00:02:05.729 --> 00:02:11.610
like millions of Italian voters

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:17.790
jeff has turned his back on mainstream
political parties. He now campaigns for

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:22.560
the populist five star movement its
sought to build a following less through

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.000
policies and more by challenging
everything about italy's political class

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:58.670
Five Star's anti-establishment message is
resonating with voters

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:04.760
it is now Italy's biggest opposition
party the country has been crippled by

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:10.310
recession and stagnating wages with 
rates of inequality among the highest

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:15.680
in Europe many people feel left behind
by globalization and let down by

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:22.310
political leaders now the populist sense
there may be an opportunity to bring

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:26.430
those leaders down
a referendum on constitutional reform

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:31.850
has become a vote of confidence in the
ruling elite

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:42.500
Prime Minister Matteo Renzi has said he
will resign if the country votes no

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:56.000
He's the latest politician to find himself in the firing line

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:07.550
tonight thousands of five-star
supporters are gathering at a rally in

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:12.700
Turin some are starting to ask what they
might do with success

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:38.680
Virginia Raggi is one of the first leaders leaders of five-star to win power as the
new mayor of Rome she's already under

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:43.280
pressure to offer actual solutions

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:07.180
But Raggi is just the warm-up act there's one man that
everyone has turned out to see

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:11.949
Five stars leader and showman Beppe Grillo

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:19.710
A former stand-up comedian Grillo knows
the buttons to press. It's his appeal to

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:25.440
peoples emotions that has helped turn
five star into a real force

00:05:39.569 --> 00:05:44.860
Beppe Grillo has vowed to get rid of
political parties but he certainly knows

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:47.819
how to start one

00:05:54.729 --> 00:05:59.680
Grillo's success has come through
impassioned charges against the corrupt

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:05.500
elites and global forces he blames for
Italy's woes but five stars leaders may

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:09.599
soon have a harder note to hear a

00:06:09.659 --> 00:06:15.150
question of how they would tackle
unemployment and inequality

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:22.800
two days after the rally Italians
overwhelmingly voted no in the

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:28.760
referendum Prime Minister Renzi made
good on his promise to stand down

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:34.020
it's another victory for populism as
across the world charismatic leaders

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:39.660
defy expectations they're finding
success selling deceptively simple

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:45.780
answers to difficult questions

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:56.580
they almost always blame

00:06:56.580 --> 00:07:02.490
the failings of free trade and mass
migration for rising inequality but is

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:10.379
this the right target

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:17.819
few cities are immune to the uneven
impact of globalization here in San

00:07:17.819 --> 00:07:23.430
Francisco is another more conspicuous
driver of change it's not just trade

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:29.030
that's transforming the global economic
order it's technology

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:35.630
the latest venture from a San Francisco
startup has the potential to turn one of

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:39.870
America's most iconic industries on its
head

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:46.290
last year uber paid 680 million dollars
for Otto a company whose technology

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:52.290
could fundamentally change trucking
forever it allows a truck to drive

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:56.810
down a highway with nobody at the wheel

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:01.460
the company claims it could save the
industry billions of dollars a year

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:06.060
reduce emissions by a third and
eliminate the driver errors that cause

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:18.279
up to 87% of truck crashes but this bright
sounding future has a dark side

00:08:18.279 --> 00:08:26.109
a series of studies have found
technology not globalization to be the

00:08:26.109 --> 00:08:30.839
biggest driver of inequality in
developed countries

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:37.380
there were three and a half million
people employed in trucking in America

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:42.760
and with their industry seemingly the next
in line for automation many face an

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:45.810
uncertain future

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:52.749
Robert Calista has driven trucks since
the 1980s both his parents were truck

00:08:52.749 --> 00:08:59.589
drivers before him

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:14.579
populist leaders have been able to
capitalize on a growing sense of them

00:10:14.579 --> 00:10:21.720
and us as inequality grows in Western
democracies wealthy California has

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:26.970
become one of the most economically
unequal states in America as technology

00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:31.189
has displaced many lower skilled jobs

00:10:33.319 --> 00:10:38.550
Russell Hancock runs a think-tank in
Silicon Valley sponsored by some of the

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:45.320
state's biggest tech companies

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:15.800
An alienated public turned on the

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:19.020
establishment because it failed to
provide answers

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:24.240
as some tech giants become as powerful
as that establishment it's a lesson

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:33.660
they're starting to learn so they're
going back to school if technological

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:38.370
change is part of the problem the people
behind it are asking how they can offer

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:40.940
solutions

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:55.459
Hadi Partovi is the CEO of code.org

00:11:55.459 --> 00:12:00.390
backed by some of Silicon Valley's
biggest firms he campaigns for children

00:12:00.390 --> 00:12:05.780
to be taught computer science in schools

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:12.840
It will need help from governments and business to ensure retraining isn't an option reserved for
those with the time and resources

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:18.699
technology itself can help too
Sebastian Thrun used to be in charge of

00:13:18.699 --> 00:13:23.919
Google's self-driving car project now he
runs an education company offering quick

00:13:23.919 --> 00:13:28.689
training programs online

00:13:51.999 --> 00:13:58.150
an ongoing online education could be one

00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:02.230
way to start relieving the pressure on
people who today feel left behind

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:07.120
because in the long run technology has
the potential to create more jobs than

00:14:07.120 --> 00:14:13.080
it destroys

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:39.300
For too many people in western democracies
progress is still something that happens

00:14:39.300 --> 00:14:43.040
to other people
wealth does not spread itself an

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:49.650
underclass appears beyond help finding a
way to reconnect with them and provide

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:53.550
an alternative to populism will be at
the top of the agenda for the political

00:14:53.550 --> 00:14:57.650
and business leaders of tomorrow

